  "claim": "Peter Wooldridge Townsend Equerry to a British monarch was married to a Marchioness Camden.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden. Sentence: Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden (9 May 1921 – 27 February 2004), born Cecil Rosemary Pawle, was a British socialite and artist, best known as the first wife of Group Captain Peter Townsend, who later became romantically involved with Princess Margaret of the United Kingdom.\nPage: Peter Townsend (RAF officer). Sentence: Group Captain Peter Wooldridge Townsend, (22 November 1914 – 19 June 1995) was a Royal Air Force officer, flying ace, courtier and author.\nPage: Peter Townsend (RAF officer). Sentence: He was Equerry to King George VI from 1944 to 1952 and held the same position for Queen Elizabeth II from 1952 to 1953.",
