        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden; Peter Townsend; Princess Margaret; King George VI; Queen Elizabeth II\n- Roles: British socialite; artist; Royal Air Force officer; flying ace; courtier; author; Equerry\n\nFacts:\n- Peter Townsend was born on 22 November 1914 and died on 19 June 1995.\n- Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden, was born Cecil Rosemary Pawle on 9 May 1921 and died on 27 February 2004.\n- Peter Townsend was a Royal Air Force officer, flying ace, courtier, and author.\n- Peter Townsend served as Equerry to King George VI from 1944 to 1952.\n- Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden, was a British socialite and artist.\n- Peter Townsend served as Equerry to Queen Elizabeth II from 1952 to 1953.\n- Rosemary Pratt, Marchioness Camden, was the first wife of Peter Townsend.\n- Peter Townsend later became romantically involved with Princess Margaret of the United Kingdom.",
